{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>And you shall write on them all the words of this Torah.</b> This indicates that the entire Torah was written on them, and thus the Ramban wrote: for we find in the book Tagi that the entire Torah was written on them, from בראשית onward, with its crowns and ornaments, and from there it was copied. Thus far." "<b>However,</b> our master Saadiah Gaon, of blessed memory, wrote that what was written on them was the enumeration of the commandments, just as they are written in the Halakhot Gedolot, in the manner of the azharot." "<b>That you may come into the land.</b> For the sake of this Torah you come into the land — He gives a reason for the commandment of setting up the stones, for we merited inheritance of the land only by virtue of the Torah; thus the Ramban, of blessed memory, explained. And for this reason the Sages, of blessed memory, established the mention of Torah in the blessing of the land. And it is possible to interpret 'that you may come into the land' as 'so that you may be able to come' — that is, what I command you, to write on them all the Torah, is so that you will have the power to come into the land, for the power of the Torah will vanquish the enemies who are in the land and cause it to be inherited by us."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 27, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:51:30.351263990Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}